 give Dunlap a small lead, but most are Democratic-sponsored, the effective sample is thin, and no independent survey has run since mid-October. Markets price LePage as the favorite and the most established raters call the open seat Lean Republican, so a very narrow LePage edge with wide uncertainty best balances the conflicting signals.", "watch": "Fresh independent polling in the final week, or movement among rural moderates after the King endorsement and the residency attacks, could tip the narrow edge either way.", "confidence": "low", "notes": ["Open seat: Jared Golden (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Maine's 2nd District is an open seat after Jared Golden's retirement, and both parties treat it as a top pickup opportunity. The district leans Republican by about four points, but the national environment favors Democrats, and polls since August show Matthew Dunlap holding narrow leads, including a six-point edge from the University of New Hampshire. Most of that polling, however, comes from Democratic sponsors, and no independent survey has been published since mid-October.\n\nPaul LePage, a former two-term governor with strong name recognition here, holds more cash on hand, and outside groups have spent heavily against both nominees. Prediction markets favor LePage, pricing his odds in the mid-fifties to mid-sixties, and Cook, Inside Elections and Sabato's Crystal Ball rate the race Lean Republican while other analysts call it a tossup. The forecast lands on a very narrow LePage edge with wide uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4239, "margin": -1.15}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.38, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3812, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.377, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.3179, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4062, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.4214, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.437, "ma